{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527525-w5-returning-what-was-taken","id":1527525,"title":"[W5] Returning What Was Taken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-27T18:03:49-08:00","id":1527525,"title":"[W5] Returning What Was Taken","content":"I have some thoughts on rules approaches for W5 and how to reintroduce concepts that it threw out with the bathwater. I have to stress, however, that I do not have a copy of W5 in electronica or paper, only the pdfs of V5 and H5 from that Humble Bundle promotion that they had a few months back, so I'm not sure what might be retreading ground or not. You can pretty well assume that my suggestion for accommodating these changes, however, is &quot;get rid of Harano/Hauglosk&quot;. In fact, even if you don't use them, I'd still suggest getting rid of Harano and Hauglosk as degeneration mechanics!<br /> <br /> Primal-Urge<br /> <br /> At the top of the list is adding in a kind of &quot;power stat&quot;, in the form of Primal-Urge. PU then takes over most shapeshifting from Rage, as it used to, in the form of Primal-Urge + Resolve rolls. It also adds a bonus to some of the less beefy forms to make them really good at an aspect of conflict, which for Homid involves getting people to talk by loosening up (social engineering, in other words), and for Glabro and Lupus involves taking advantage of cover, artificial and natural, respectively, to hide or to duck behind to avoid attacks. Crinos and Hispo do kind of get a benefit from it, but this is rolled in with frenzy changes.<br /> <br /> Breeds (&quot;Birth&quot;)<br /> <br /> If you're keeping the Crinos-born as disabled, my suggestion for a name-switch would be a reference to a certain smith god using the Roman name to match the mostly-Latin naming scheme of forms. So, it's Volcanus, not a certain titaness that bore Athena in Zeus's head. Also, I dispensed with &quot;breed&quot; in favor of &quot;Birth&quot;, as in Birth Form, to step around the name of the Crinos-born in one way if not another. Those born in Crinos and Lupus also recover from disconnection (q.v.) more easily, but I haven't hammered out quite by how much.<br /> <br /> Regeneration<br /> <br /> Garou aren\u2019t some kind of unliving offense to Gaia that has to \u201crouse\u201d a stolen force in order to heal \u2013 it just happens. Outside of their Birth forms, with the exception of those born in Crinos, a Garou will heal two superficial levels of damage per turn. In any given form, she will heal one aggravated level per day. No roll is required.<br /> <br /> Up next is how to handle the Garou's spirit side. I'm assuming that you're dumping Umbral damage and the need to use a rite to enter the Umbra, incidentally.<br /> <br /> Disconnection<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> While suffused with Umbral energies as half-spirit beings, Garou do not possess an infinite well of these reserves. When calling upon Gifts, appeasing spirits, or otherwise expending spiritual energy, the character must check to see if there is a widening gap in her proximity to her spiritual side.<br /> Disconnection ranges from 0, where the Garou is incredibly spiritually in-tune and vital, to 5, which sees her looking inexplicably worn out regardless of her physical health and a pale, flickering shadow when in the Umbra, which can become a difficult place to get to while in this state.<br /> Calling upon spiritual energy to accomplish a task is an Essence roll, which can accomplish a great many things but always entails rolling a single die. A success (result of 6+) does not result in a noticeable increase in Disconnection. Failure increases Disconnection by 1. Essence rolls cannot take place in the same turn that the character spends a level of Rage, and vice versa, unless a Gift calls for it.<br /> <br /> Effects of Disconnection<br /> <br /> Being disconnected makes passage through the Umbra more difficult, and each point increases the time necessary to Step Sideways by one turn. Disconnection also acts as a negative dice pool modifier to rolls to sense spiritual presences or to utilize subtler and more introspective Gifts.<br /> <br /> Recovering from Disconnection<br /> <br /> The most common way to recover from being worn of spiritual energies is to meditate in a spiritually compatible place, preferably in a caern. Roll the character\u2019s Primal-Urge + Composure + Caern Rating; every two successes alleviates a point of Disconnection. This can only be accomplished once per day, and meditation over concurrent days increases the required successes by one per the total number of days relying on this method.<br /> <br /> Another method is known as the Sacred Hunt, where a form of spiritual prey is pursued by all the members of a sept. At the conclusion of the rite, all Garou who participated alleviate all levels of Disconnection.<br /> <br /> Finally, spirits can be cajoled to directly supply their reserves. Provided that the werewolf has not requested it of any spirits for an entire month, she may make a persuasion roll, modified by the temperament and attitude that a spirit has for her. Each success allows her to alleviate one point of Disconnection.<br /> <br /> Causes of Disconnection:<br /> <br /> Utilizing various spiritual powers (number of checks dependent on Gift or other power)<br /> <br /> Not stepping sideways into the Umbra for a year (check every year, on the same day of the year).<br /> <br /> Subsisting on highly processed foods for a month (check repeats monthly).<br /> <br /> Not saving a wolf from human actions or Triatic minions (check each incident). Fera swap this out for the appropriate animal of their kind.\u200b</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rage<br /> <br /> This is, by far, the largest section. I'll divide it up.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Rage is a state of inhuman fury that Garou nearly always fall into, at least on some level. There are six discrete levels of Rage that werewolves can experience, ranging from Calm, a state that few, if any, werewolves feel for an extended period of time, to Apoplectic, where the character is constantly on the edge of frenzy but still maintaining tenuous control. Intensifying Rage involves hurt, shame, embarrassment, or other intense emotions, while decreasing it typically requires venting this ferocity toward a specific end. Completely losing control and sliding into a frenzy is the ultimate form of this venting, though it is also possible for Rage to level off until finding a scene full of aggravating circumstances and individuals.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Levels of Rage<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 0 \u2013 Calm: The Garou is mostly unhindered by any hints of inhuman anger \u2013 but can still be normally angry. There are no mechanical differences with the \u201cnormal\u201d state to note other than that if some stimulus provokes a frenzy in the character, she gains a +2 bonus to resist\u2026 but even if she resists successfully, her Rage increases by one level.<br /> <br /> 1 \u2013 Vexed: Starting here, the werewolf begins to experience supernatural levels of emotion\u2026 and agitation. At this level and those higher, add half of the character\u2019s Rage level, rounded up, to the difficulty to resist frenzy. However, this comes with a decidedly dangerous upside, in that the Garou can apply their Defense against Firearms attacks without penalty even without cover.<br /> <br /> 2 \u2013 Furious: The Garou can now add her Rage level to Dexterity + Athletics tests out of combat, or once per turn in combat. She may also reduce her Rage level to apply this bonus to every Dexterity + Athletics test she makes in combat until her next turn.<br /> <br /> 3 \u2013 Fiery: By taking a Dexterity + Athletics test to move, the Garou can move up to ten yards per point of Rage, passing the distance as if flashing between two spaces. If she lowers her Rage rating by one, she does not need to roll and may move in this fashion up to her Dexterity times before her next turn. This movement can be accomplished in any direction, so long as the werewolf has the means to do so.<br /> <br /> 4 \u2013 Raving: At this point, the character must resist going into a frenzy over more inconsequential inconveniences, such as being informed of delays or setbacks, having her way blocked by unfamiliar individuals, or simply being confronted by non-Garou authority figures. However, she may also attack every opposed character in close combat with a single attack, or make two attacks against a single close combat target.<br /> <br /> 5 \u2013 Apoplectic: The werewolf must resist frenzy every turn while in combat, or every scene while out of it. It is plainly obvious that she is dangerous, due to her fitful breathing, ruddy countenance, clenched jaw, and pulsing veins. However, this feverish state also allows her to casually oppose the extreme speed of those that would normally deny her an effort to defend herself, such as certain vampires. By opting to make two attacks against everyone in arm\u2019s reach or three attacks against an individual, she can vent this level of Rage and lower her rating back to being only Raving.<br /> <br /> Spending Levels of Rage<br /> <br /> While some levels of Rage have unique expenditure circumstances, Garou at any levels of Rage above 0 can shed one level to do one of the following:<br /> <br /> Activate a Gift that requires one or more levels of Rage (no spending levels that you don\u2019t have).<br /> Ignore the result of being stunned in combat.<br /> Instantly change to any other form without the need to roll.<br /> Recover from being at Incapacitated or lower health. This automatically causes the character to frenzy but restores her to her last two health levels regardless of how many more she should be suffering, which can save her not only from being inactive but also from dying. This option can only be used once per scene.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Gaining Rage<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Upon seeing the moon the first time since she last woke up, the Garou gains a level of Rage. If it is her auspice moon, she gains two levels.<br /> <br /> Critical Failures and other humiliating experiences roll a variable number of dice, from one to five. Each success increases the character\u2019s Rage level by one.<br /> <br /> Betrayal can sting straight through to the soul. Experiencing it from a close character such as a packmate or touchstone increases the character\u2019s Rage by two levels.<br /> <br /> If suddenly thrown into a tense situation from rest, the Garou gains one Rage level.<br /> <br /> If a Garou would gain Rage but is already Apoplectic, she remains at the same level but can gain the benefit of expending as many levels of Rage as she would have gained without actually decreasing it. It also requires a frenzy roll at a -2 penalty.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Consequences of Rage<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Rage is not a subtle thing, and its temperamental nature makes those without it wary and fearful of those who do \u2013 and they can feel it radiating off of Garou and others like them, like a wash of heat on a road in the sun.<br /> <br /> For every point of Rage presently higher than the character\u2019s Composure, she takes a penalty to all Social rolls not geared toward frightening others or, oddly enough, unhinged carousing.<br /> <br /> If a character\u2019s Primal-Urge + present Rage are higher than a non-Kinfolk human or animal\u2019s Willpower, they feel ill at ease around the werewolf and will seek to avoid her. This is known as the Curse, and tends to make life among normal humans or wolves difficult. Kinfolk frequently act as intermediaries, where a pool of highly focused and unflappable workers is not available.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Frenzy<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> There are two ways that Rage overcomes Garou \u2013 the berserk frenzy, in which the werewolf assumes Crinos, stands and fights (or typically slaughters and massacres); and the fox frenzy, where Rage fans the flame of fear and causes the Garou to change into Lupus and flee with all speed. Resisting either state requires a Willpower test. Characters are not out of the control of the player, technically, in either case, but the player is obligated to play out a character who is out of control, and out of control really means out of control. Having a Primal-Urge at least equal to the current level of Rage can keep the werewolf from attacking members of their pack, but that\u2019s mostly the extent of control, barring Gifts that alter the way frenzy works.<br /> <br /> Berserk frenzies last until enemies or the Garou are dead. Fox frenzies last until after the Garou manages to flee, evade any pursuers, and hide for at least a scene. Garou tend to be much more susceptible to going berserk than being overtaken by the fox; generally, only the most hopeless situations stir the latter significantly enough for it to require a roll. Additionally, if any opposing forces are armed with silver, increase the difficulty of any of these triggers, berserk or fox, by one.<br /> <br /> Sample berserk frenzy triggers:<br /> <br /> Provocation<br /> Difficulty<br /> Friend injured by an aggressor<br /> 2 (serious injury 3, killed 4)<br /> Lover or Touchstone injured by an aggressor<br /> 3 (serious injury 4, killed 5)<br /> Packmate injured by an aggressor not in the pack<br /> 4 (serious injury 5, killed 6)<br /> Insulted<br /> 2 (by perceived inferior 3)<br /> Public Humilation<br /> 2 (3 if in front of higher-Ranked character)<br /> First injury in fight<br /> 1 (serious injury 2, injury that would be lethal to a human 3)<br /> <br /> Sample fox frenzy triggers:<br /> <br /> Provocation<br /> Difficulty<br /> Excessively weird circumstance outside of comfort zone (without pack present)<br /> 1<br /> Confronting a Nexus Crawler (re-check each time it warps reality)<br /> 2<br /> All other packmates die in battle<br /> 3<br /> Confronting a Maeljin Incarna or Talon of the Wyrm<br /> 4 (5 in Malfeas)<br /> Confronting a Triatic Wyrm Avatar<br /> 5 (7 in Malfeas)<br /> <br /> A Garou can temper their actions in frenzy for a turn by spending a Willpower point. After spending three such points, the frenzy breaks and the character is considered to have shaken it off and cleared her head. However, while in a berserk frenzy, if the Garou kills an opponent, roll Composure. A critical failure indicates that she stops fighting for a turn to begin eating that unfortunate. If the character has lingered in Crinos for days without eating sufficiently larger meals, this occurs on a simple failure. Only grossly inedible characters will be passed over, in favor of the nearest likely-edible character. On the next turn, repeat the roll; a failure indicates that she continues eating, while a success snaps her out of it and puts her back in the fight.<br /> <br /> When not tempering her actions, a Garou gain a bonus to frenzy-viable actions equal to her Primal-Urge value, a like penalty to actions that aren\u2019t supported by the frenzy, and double that penalty for actions that go against the character of a frenzy (if the dice pool is reduced to 0 or lower, the action cannot be attempted). The character of a frenzy involves turning non-packmates nearby into piles of meat or scrap on the ground or pursuing nearby non-packmates for berserk frenzies; for a fox frenzy, the bonus applies to actions that would put you further away from whatever prompted it, which can include fighting if there is no other way out, but a fox frenzy prioritizes escape over that; only actual unavoidable fights will receive the bonus, and the Garou will also be more concerned about making sure that the other party won\u2019t be able to pursue them than with necessarily killing them; a quick, crippling blow over a sustained fight, in other words.<br /> <br /> At no point is it necessary to remove the player from control of their character; if, for whatever reason, the player keeps attempting to undertake penalized actions with dice pools above 0, the lack of success should stand on its own. Talk out any differences over declaring the actions of the player\u2019s character.\u200b</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And now for an adaptation of 13th Age's Escalation Die and Aberrant 2e's Collateral pool...<br /> <br /> Carnage<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> This track, running from 1 to 10, denotes the level of danger in the present scene. It should not be used for every scene; combat is a sure one, and also highly strained negotiations, but it can be omitted if the Storyteller and players feel that it wouldn't fit. For scenes where it is used, it is a narrative tool that helps to guide the horrifying violence that follows Garou and Fera around like their own shadows. Specifically, it\u2019s all about turning otherwise nondescript levels of damage into maiming and dismemberment. The Garou can, of course, heal this damage easily, but it still hurts like hell. Humans, naturally, are out of luck, and even vampires are in for an unpleasant time if they hang around werewolves, assuming that they don't simply end up suffering the final death.<br /> <br /> For every turn that any Garou in the scene spends in Crinos or Hispo, increase the Carnage counter by one (or two in an uncontrolled berserk frenzy). If particularly hazardous weapons or substances are present, such as high explosives or intense harmful environmental hazards, increase the count by one or more per use or turn as appropriate. The count stops at 10, unless you\u2019re in a hopeless situation against godlike entities, where it usually starts at 5 and might not have a ceiling.<br /> <br /> When no characters are in Crinos or Hispo and no attacks occur, reduce the Carnage track by one. One or more characters entering fox frenzy will also reduce the Carnage value by one per turn of unrestrained flight.<br /> <br /> When Carnage is in play, crippling injuries are the norm, even for superficial damage (count superficial damage as half its value in aggravated for these purposes). Instead of rolling a d10, add the present Carnage rating. Note that for Garou, Fera, and spirits, 13+ denotes incapacitated but still able to regenerate. It does increase the difficulty to avoid battle scars by 1 each time in a scene it occurs, however. In this state, any additional damage can be terminal for changers, barring a typical roll for recovery.<br /> <br /> While Garou and Fera can regenerate from lost limbs, this isn\u2019t certain. Roll Primal-Urge at the end of the scene, with a difficulty of 3 if the character used Rage to recover from being incapacitated or killed. Failure means that she fails to recover from the most severe injury.\u200b</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And here's something that plays into truly old school loresheets...<br /> <br /> Rituals and Rites \u2013 A System Topic<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The bedrock of Garou society, knowledge of their customs and practices also give rise to what outsiders would potentially consider \u201cmagic\u201d, though to the Garou, they are a sacred part of their spiritual world. Each point of this loresheet must be purchased concurrently, i.e. no two dot level without the first, no third without the second, etc. Fera will also possess this Loresheet, but for their own specific culture and practices.<br /> <br /> Lore<br /> <br /> 1 \u2013 You have likely just been introduced to Garou culture and have some idea about why it is they perform some ceremonies. Some key utility rites are available, such as Talisman Dedication or Purification.<br /> 2 \u2013 A solid working knowledge and practice of how to function in Garou society. You can perform more advanced rites such as summoning spirits.<br /> 3 \u2013 Beginning to dive into the more advanced and esoteric elements of being Garou, you can lead some of the more significant ceremonies during a moot for your own tribe. At this level of knowledge, you might be able to seriously punish lawbreakers to your culture, or reach an agreement with a spirit for it to empower a talisman or instrument.<br /> 4 \u2013 Your knowledge reaches even other tribes of Garou, allowing you to handle moots at even multi-tribe septs. Rites at this level include tying your perceptions to your sept\u2019s territory or conceal it from interlopers.<br /> 5 \u2013 You\u2019re certainly the apprentice to your sept\u2019s Master of the Rite, and you might even be able to build a new caern, or empower a legendary hero with greater power from the Umbra in recognition for their nigh-impossible deeds.<br /> <br /> *Bonus: Your rating in Rituals is equal to the highest level of this Loresheet that you have purchased, and comes with one rite of that level or lower.\u200b</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (Like a broken record, I'd also suggest ditching everything about rites in W5 in favor of a legacy edition. This just facilitates that with a pseudo-skill a la Weapons of the Gods kung fu styles and pseudo-skills.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T18:19:59-08:00","id":1527530,"title":"","content":"There's some interesting arguments whenever these retcons come up about how you might incorporate them in-universe.<br /> <br /> One idea I had was in 2004 that Gaia turned all of the Kinfolk of the Garou Nation into Garou.<br /> <br /> And, well, their numbers have been going straight down ever since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T18:42:51-08:00","id":1527531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527525-w5-returning-what-was-taken?p=1527530#post1527530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some interesting arguments whenever these retcons come up about how you might incorporate them in-universe.<br /> <br /> One idea I had was in 2004 that Gaia turned all of the Kinfolk of the Garou Nation into Garou.<br /> <br /> And, well, their numbers have been going straight down ever since.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the storylines from Apocalypse run longer than 2004, so probably not immediately then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T23:14:32-08:00","id":1527535,"title":"","content":"Not to sound flippant, but why bother? It seems obvious you don't like W5 at all, so why make the effort? Wouldn't your time be better spent on fixing those things in W20/Revised you think are problematic instead of completely overhauling a system you don't care for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T01:13:20-08:00","id":1527538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527525-w5-returning-what-was-taken?p=1527535#post1527535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to sound flippant, but why bother? It seems obvious you don't like W5 at all, so why make the effort? Wouldn't your time be better spent on fixing those things in W20/Revised you think are problematic instead of completely overhauling a system you don't care for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a lot of us want W5 to be more functional and going through where it fails can be a good discussion on WHY it fails and so what not to do.<br /> <br /> I've said it multiple times but here goes again; The idea of W5 is not bad, the issues arise from it being disjointed and suffering from being passed from team to team for over 8 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T02:18:02-08:00","id":1527542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527525-w5-returning-what-was-taken?p=1527538#post1527538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because a lot of us want W5 to be more functional and going through where it fails can be a good discussion on WHY it fails and so what not to do.<br /> <br /> I've said it multiple times but here goes again; The idea of W5 is not bad, the issues arise from it being disjointed and suffering from being passed from team to team for over 8 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> For me, there is a line between house-ruling the current system to be better suit my needs and preferences and outright rewriting core design assumptions behind 5th edition. Having special dice that somehow enforce a game's theme is one of the core design assumptions I have with WOD5. That's where OP's ideas fail for me; they don't feel like 5th edition to me. YMMV, of course. Still, if I were to be asked to play in a W5 chronicle, I'd pass if I saw the rewrites above.<br /> <br /> Everyone's different and has different tastes, though, so I'll keep out of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T08:40:21-08:00","id":1527553,"title":"","content":"I viewed the special dice replacing part of a pool as less a unifying mechanic for all WoD games in an edition and more just V5 and H5 spinning their wheels. Given that Garou and Fera can also escalate the scale of physical confrontations into uncomfortably high stakes, I thought it better to try and reflect a state where getting into a serious fight would involve an escalating series of horrifying injuries that could see just about anyone getting to within a hair's breadth of dying and could leave them with permanent injuries.<br /> <br /> As for the Rage levels, I just thought it might add some texture to riding closer to absolute fury. I'd be up to tweaking that, but not in making Rage work like Hunger. That just seems backward; you're gaining Rage in situations where legacy would require spending it i.e. venting it and lowering the value. Is there even any mechanic that related Rage to, well, actually being enraged?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T08:59:46-08:00","id":1527556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527525-w5-returning-what-was-taken?p=1527535#post1527535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to sound flippant, but why bother? It seems obvious you don't like W5 at all, so why make the effort? Wouldn't your time be better spent on fixing those things in W20/Revised you think are problematic instead of completely overhauling a system you don't care for?</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise we didn't lynch you for your ideas about tinkering with w5 and building up new mechanics? Just because you don't care for these changes doesn't make them invalid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T09:56:39-08:00","id":1527558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527525-w5-returning-what-was-taken?p=1527556#post1527556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realise we didn't lynch you for your ideas about tinkering with w5 and building up new mechanics? Just because you don't care for these changes doesn't make them invalid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure SOS doesn't feel &quot;lynched&quot; by my comments.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't appreciate your tone-policing. You put stuff out here, you get people's opinion on it. These forums aren't exactly kind to those who have minority opinions. I accept that, but that street goes both ways. Anyway, I only responded because you addressed me personally. I don't want to derail this thread any further and won't reply again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T17:16:20-08:00","id":1527645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527525-w5-returning-what-was-taken?p=1527535#post1527535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to sound flippant, but why bother? It seems obvious you don't like W5 at all, so why make the effort? Wouldn't your time be better spent on fixing those things in W20/Revised you think are problematic instead of completely overhauling a system you don't care for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to have another crack at making the W20 rules a little less messy, maybe even basically use Revised Storyteller if I ever get to run it. I'm personally sticking with W20 because I find it problematic but can tell what kind of game it is, but some people might prefer the mechanics of W5 enough to put the things they're missing back in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although IIRC shape shifting was always tied to Rage. I'm fairly certain that healing quickly enough for it to matter in combat was also tied to Rage, I should really pull my book out.<br /> <br /> As to the crinos-born/metis, I'm not 100% on board with vulcanus as a replacement term. At least to me it makes me think of an affinity for something before I think of disabilities. Honestly I wonder if it's better to have them straight up lack a proper bread name, to help emphasize their situation.<br /> <br /> Totally agreed on Birth Form being better than Breed, I'd also use First Form and maybe a pretentious equivalent based on a dead of foreign language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T18:05:16-08:00","id":1527647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1527525-w5-returning-what-was-taken?p=1527645#post1527645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really need to have another crack at making the W20 rules a little less messy, maybe even basically use Revised Storyteller if I ever get to run it. I'm personally sticking with W20 because I find it problematic but can tell what kind of game it is, but some people might prefer the mechanics of W5 enough to put the things they're missing back in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although IIRC shape shifting was always tied to Rage. I'm fairly certain that healing quickly enough for it to matter in combat was also tied to Rage, I should really pull my book out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You automatically regenerated a bashing level per turn, or one lethal if you made a Stamina (difficulty 8) roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to the crinos-born/metis, I'm not 100% on board with vulcanus as a replacement term. At least to me it makes me think of an affinity for something before I think of disabilities. Honestly I wonder if it's better to have them straight up lack a proper bread name, to help emphasize their situation. </div> </div> </div>I did note that it was a modern term deriving from the same Latin-ish fad that named Homid and Lupus. None of them are going to be really well-fitting. With Vulcan/Hephaestus, there are stories where they dealt with him the Spartan way because he had congenital issues, only for him to survive and end up getting back up to Olympus only because of utilitarian value.<br /> <br /> (I'm aware that other stories attribute his issues to getting between Zeus and Hera during a fight and ending up permanently injured that way. In terms of myths, it probably still fits.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Totally agreed on Birth Form being better than Breed, I'd also use First Form and maybe a pretentious equivalent based on a dead of foreign language. </div> </div> </div>Not that W5 wants us to have old forms of anything...<br /> <br /> (At the moment, I'm watching the MSt3K marathon, and they just reached the end pitch by Crow about pitching The Final Sacrifice as a TV Series. Executive meddling aplenty! Just like with the WoD!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}